-- title:
--   Uniqueness of the Hecke multiplier on the ℓ-degeneracy roof
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $K$ an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, let $N\ge 1$ satisfy $(N:K)\neq 0$, and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq p$. Write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldC K N` for the $K$-subfield $K(j(q),j(q^N))$ of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated by the two $q$-expansions `jqModC K` and `jqNModC K N`, and $R=$ `charLDegeneracyRoof K N ℓ` for the $K$-subfield $K(j(q),j(q^N),j(q^{\ell}),j(q^{N\ell}))$, so that $F\subseteq R$. Two $K$-algebra maps $F\to R$ are in play: $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC K N ℓ`, the inclusion, and $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC K N ℓ`, induced by the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$ on Laurent series. Let $x=$ `jGeomGen K N` be $j(q)$ regarded as an element of $F$. Suppose $h\in R$ satisfies, with $R$ given the $F$-algebra structure along $\alpha$ and the resulting tower $K\subseteq F\subseteq R$, the identity $d_{R/K}(\beta x)=h\cdot \alpha^{*}\bigl(d_{F/K}x\bigr)$ in $\Omega_{R/K}$, where $\alpha^{*}$ is the functorial map $\Omega_{F/K}\to\Omega_{R/K}$. Then $h$ equals [`ModularCurve.heckeMultiplier N K ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_SSHeckeV2.html#L20), the element of $R$ chosen by `Classical.epsilon` as a solution of exactly this equation.
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the defining property of the Hecke multiplier attached to the two degeneracy maps $\alpha,\beta$ of the $\ell$-degeneracy roof: any element of $R$ satisfying the differential identity is the chosen multiplier, so statements that characterise an element by that identity may be transferred to the canonical choice. It is used in the computation of the leading term of the trace along $\beta$ that identifies the Hecke operator in characteristic $p$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_SSHeckeV2_eq_heckeMultiplier_of_D_heckeBetaC_eq_smul_map.lean

